<main class="pc" data-product-depth="c0-c1"><p class="pc-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS / Research / Anatomical diagram · illustration</p><h1>C0–C1–C2: three levels of one region.</h1><p class="pc-lead">Explore skeletal landmarks of the craniovertebral region and questions about their relative orientation.</p><div class="pc-steps" role="navigation" aria-label="Research"><a href="../primordocciput/">Primordocciput</a><a href="../c0-c1/" aria-current="page">C0–C1–C2</a><a href="../logbook/">Logbook</a></div><section class="pc-section"><div class="pc-feature pc-levels"><svg viewBox="0 0 320 280" role="img" aria-label="C0 C1 C2 schematic"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".24"><path d="M160 12V270M22 80H298M22 145H298M22 211H298" stroke-dasharray="4 6"/></g><g fill="none" stroke="var(--pa)" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M78 34Q160 6 242 34L230 67Q160 94 90 67Z"/><ellipse cx="160" cy="138" rx="64" ry="20"/><path d="M112 200L145 188L151 162H169L175 188L208 200L193 230H127Z"/></g><g fill="currentColor" font-size="15"><text x="252" y="55">C0</text><text x="237" y="143">C1</text><text x="222" y="215">C2</text></g></svg><div><details open><summary>C0</summary><p>Occipital bone — C0 (notation in the CRANIO model).</p></details><details><summary>C1</summary><p>Atlas — first cervical vertebra.</p></details><details><summary>C2</summary><p>Axis — second cervical vertebra.</p></details><p class="pc-note">Schematic levels, not an image of individual anatomy. External asymmetry alone does not determine relative bone position.</p><a class="pc-button" href="../configuration/">Explore configuration ↗</a></div></div></section><section class="pc-section"><h2>Four kinds of research information</h2><div class="pc-grid"><details class="pc-card"><summary>Observed</summary><p>Describe what is visible in a particular context.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Measured</summary><p>Record units, method, conditions and uncertainty.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Reported</summary><p>Preserve the source of the subjective report.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Research concept</summary><p>State the model, question and possible test.</p></details></div><div class="pc-actions"><a class="pc-button primary" href="../start/">Discuss research collaboration</a><a class="pc-button" href="../technology/">Technology</a></div></section><section class="pc-section"><details class="pc-legacy"><summary>Existing materials</summary><div class="wrap"><article class="article"><div class="crumbs">CRANIO / C0–C1</div><h2>C0–C1: the upper cranio-cervical reference.</h2><p class="lead">C0 is the occipital base of the skull; C1 is the atlas.</p><section class="section"><div class="eyebrow">C0–C1</div><h2>C0–C1: the upper cranio-cervical reference.</h2><p class="lead">C0 is the occipital base of the skull; C1 is the atlas.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>Observation</h3><p>Separate observation from interpretation.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Context</h3><p>Context makes a state comparable over time.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Verification</h3><p>Before, after, context and time remain visible.</p></div></div></section><div class="actions"><a class="btn dark" href="../start/">Start an observation</a><a class="btn" href="../explore/">Explore</a></div></article></div></details></section></main>